88efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40.bin","sha256":"b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40"}},{"id":"dfe67f6cb307a6b46188692e14647aa32a9e614ba8ad0236ddbdefd2a3b257ab","quote":"The common stock dividend was $0.45 per share, compared with $0.43 per share during the second quarter of 2025. Common shares outstanding decreased 1.7 million from the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to common stock repurchases. During the second quarter of 2026, we repurchased 1.2 million common shares outstanding for $75 million. We did not repurchase any common shares during the prior year period.","context":"1 Includes amounts related to common shares acquired through our publicly announced plans and those acquired in connection with our stock compensation plan. These shares were acquired from employees to cover their payroll taxes and stock option exercise costs upon the exercise of stock options.","section":"RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":57,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000109380-26-000103","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-07-20","reportDate":"2026-07-20","cik":"0000109380","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/109380/000010938026000103/exh991earningsrelease20260.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40.bin","sha256":"b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40"}},{"id":"f2b6e011c5e17ef7e300120c4ea68a27aa8905610436febca4685a7ba43c0b66","quote":"At June 30, 2026, the accumulated other comprehensive income (loss) (“AOCI”) balance reflected a net loss of $1.9 billion, primarily attributable to a decline in the fair value of fixed-rate AFS securities driven by changes in interest rates. This amount includes $1.5 billion ($1.1 billion after tax) of unrealized losses associated with securities previously transferred from AFS to held-to-maturity (“HTM”). Compared with June 30, 2025, AOCI improved $297 million, primarily due to increases in the fair value of AFS securities, the amortization of unrealized losses associated with the securities transferred from AFS to HTM, and paydowns on AFS securities. The improvement in AOCI had a positive impact on our tangible book value per common share.","context":"The common stock dividend was $0.45 per share, compared with $0.43 per share during the second quarter of 2025. Common shares outstanding decreased 1.7 million from the second quarter of 2025, primarily due to common stock repurchases. During the second quarter of 2026, we repurchased 1.2 million common shares outstanding for $75 million. We did not repurchase any common shares during the prior year period.","section":"RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":58,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000109380-26-000103","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-07-20","reportDate":"2026-07-20","cik":"0000109380","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/109380/000010938026000103/exh991earningsrelease20260.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40.bin","sha256":"b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40"}},{"id":"370d70609bb334b5727cbd0ef41de24637a969185c83563ef8725211a6749e59","quote":"Estimated common equity tier 1 (“CET1”) capital was $8.4 billion, an increase of 11%, compared with $7.6 billion in the prior year period. The estimated CET1 capital ratio was 11.8%, compared with 11.0%. Tangible book value per common share increased 22% to $44.74, mainly due to an increase in retained earnings and reduced unrealized losses in AOCI. For more information on non-GAAP financial measures, see pages 19-22.","context":"At June 30, 2026, the accumulated other comprehensive income (loss) (“AOCI”) balance reflected a net loss of $1.9 billion, primarily attributable to a decline in the fair value of fixed-rate AFS securities driven by changes in interest rates. This amount includes $1.5 billion ($1.1 billion after tax) of unrealized losses associated with securities previously transferred from AFS to held-to-maturity (“HTM”). Compared with June 30, 2025, AOCI improved $297 million, primarily due to increases in the fair value of AFS securities, the amortization of unrealized losses associated with the securities transferred from AFS to HTM, and paydowns on AFS securities. The improvement in AOCI had a positive impact on our tangible book value per common share.","section":"RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":59,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000109380-26-000103","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-07-20","reportDate":"2026-07-20","cik":"0000109380","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/109380/000010938026000103/exh991earningsrelease20260.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40.bin","sha256":"b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40"}},{"id":"791332ad393c1a3178159099245c309315304b2eb62d3b4d45384e013511497e","quote":"Supplemental Presentation and Conference Call","context":"Press Release – Page 7","section":"RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":62,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0000109380-26-000103","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-07-20","reportDate":"2026-07-20","cik":"0000109380","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/109380/000010938026000103/exh991earningsrelease20260.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40.bin","sha256":"b0be2fb2c7ebe19d4f019b8772dd92fd7da488efae543753c3937e2cf2facf40"}},{"id":"7dd0a0ad66c99392b74a314ec72c7e618ffca3c5bdd6cff46c6e346b6fa287ec","quote":"Zions has posted a supplemental presentation to its website in advance of its discussion of second quarter financial results, scheduled